From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] leave: include <sys/types.h> for u_int

leave.c uses u_int, which it gets from <sys/types.h> through another
header. With macOS 26's headers (the SDK's and the sysroot's alike) none
of its includes reaches <sys/types.h>, so it fails to compile; include it.

--- a/leave/leave.c
+++ b/leave/leave.c
@@ -43,6 +43,8 @@
 #include <sys/cdefs.h>
 __FBSDID("$FreeBSD$");
 
+#include <sys/types.h>
+
 #include <err.h>
 #include <ctype.h>
 #include <locale.h>
